<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mentuhotep III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 2000 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century-bce">21st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mentuhotep III was a king of the Eleventh Dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, son and successor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mentuhotep-ii">Mentuhotep II</a>, who reigned about twelve years around 2000 BCE. He inherited a united and stable kingdom, built temples in the Theban region and sent an expedition under the official <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henenu">Henenu</a> across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-desert">Eastern Desert</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-sea">Red Sea</a> to sail for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/land-of-punt">Punt</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mentuhotep-iii.jpg" alt="Mentuhotep III" width="320" height="433" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Keith Schengili-Roberts · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mentuhotep-OsirideStatue-CloseUp_MuseumOfFineArtsBoston.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
